  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA dominates (0.485–0.650) while image-only is weak (0.208). Within RNA, we know scvi_n200 > pca_n2000 (0.650 vs 0.591) and avgpool > transformer (0.591 vs 0.519), both under multiprofile. The key remaining uncertainty among RNA encoders is where scgpt falls relative to scvi_n200. Question tested: config_008 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) holds profile and aggregation fixed at their best-known settings, isolating the encoder variable for a clean three-way comparison (pca_n2000 vs scvi_n200 vs scgpt). Why this is the best next experiment: RNA is the dominant signal source, so the encoder choice is the highest-leverage design decision. Resolving whether scgpt beats, matches, or trails scvi_n200 under identical conditions will either (a) confirm scvi_n200 as the optimal RNA backbone, letting us confidently move to multimodal fusion tests, or (b) reveal a superior encoder that reshapes the entire search. This is a low-variance, high-information experiment that reduces uncertainty on the most impactful axis before committing budget to the larger multimodal configuration space."
}

